    "createdAt": "2026-09-23T07:39:04.526716+00:00",
    "curatorComment": "<p>Some of my favorite gaming memories have come from playing with friends. But I often wonder whether I loved the games or just the time I spent with my friends? Then again, if a game helped create those memories, doesn't that make it a good game?<br><br>A recent wave of multiplayer games seems to have answered that question. <br><br>Often nicknamed friendslop, these games are built around having fun with friends. And that's what inspired this collection, which we're calling Social Multiplayer. I wouldn't consider every game here friendslop, but each is (arguably) made better by playing with friends.<br><br>But the Co-Op Bros spend a lot more time playing multiplayer games than I do so I was curious to hear what they thought. Thankfully, they agreed to help curate this collection. Check out their video for more about each game and how multiplayer gaming is evolving.<br><br>-Alex</p>",
    "curatorStatement": "",
